I'm Kate bachelder O'Dell I graduated  from Hillsdale in the class of 2013  and I'm an editorial writer for The Wall  Street Journal I spent a summer studying  Latin in England in high school and I  was writing my dad these emails about  what was going on and what I was up to  and he wrote back you could be a writer  and what you should do to be a writer is  to read and to write so it was just this  natural progression it was never this  aha moment if that makes sense and  Hillsdale was just a good fit for kind  of lining up that natural interest in  curiosity with some concrete  opportunities to write for the paper but  also do a lot of writing and coursework  I was the opinions editor of the  collegian which was a lot of fun it was  a very good education and how to work at  a newspaper meeting my husband at  Hillsdale has been one of my favorite  things about my experience because it's  so much a foundation of kind of the life  we share Hillsdale is also an education  and learning how to live with others  because it is being shipwrecked in rural  Michigan with 1,400 other people really  lean into those relationships and  friendships that are every bit as  formative and educational with some of  the more formal coursework I think  people think opinion writing is telling  people what you think about various  subjects the style of opinion writing  that we do at the journal is to report  the news and put it in an analytical  narrative  it's an institution it's more than 125  years old editorial pages in a sense you  are a steward of something that will  continue on long after you're done  working for it and so it's a taking care  of something it was really an exciting  wonderful honor to get this award  especially since so much of my life I  feel I owe to Hillsdale  almost silly to be receiving an award  from somebody and gave you everything  you have I'm honored but also just  amazed and kind of covered in gratitude  with it all  [Music]  you
 

